+## [18.17.0-fork.1] - 2026-11-06
+
+### Changed
+
+- Re-based the fork onto upstream v18.17.0.
+- `omp update` on a fork build now reports failures as errors and holds the install lock, like upstream's updater, so the background auto-update no longer exits the process when a fork release check fails.
+- Subagent worker threads now see the fork's default-account and account-priority pins, fallover notices and account-selection journal, and can resolve credential-pool selections, through the shared auth bridge.
+
+## [18.14.0-fork.1] - 2026-10-30
+
+### Removed
+
+- Removed the fork's auth-gateway user management: managed users and their tokens, ACL rules, credential pools, the admin and audit APIs, `omp auth-gateway user|pool|audit|tui`, the `/gateway` console, the `/settings` Gateway tab with its connection profiles, and the gateway user and usage block in `/usage`. `omp auth-gateway` is upstream's again (`serve`, `stdio`, `token`, `status`, `check`, scoped `--clients`); a gateway built from an earlier fork release keeps its `auth-gateway.db`, but this build no longer reads it.
+
+### Changed
+
+- Re-based the fork onto upstream v18.14.0.
+- A `/v1/models` row that states its reasoning ladder in OpenRouter's shape (`reasoning: { supported_efforts, default_effort, mandatory }`, as aigw2 serves it) now goes through upstream's advertised-reasoning discovery: `discovery.advertisedReasoning: false` turns it off, `minimal` is no longer offered, and `mandatory` keeps thinking from being switched off. The omp auth-gateway's `thinking_efforts` field is no longer read.
+
+## [18.12.2-fork.2] - 2026-10-21
+
+### Fixed
+
+- `git worktree add` in bash, `omp worktree add`, `/wt` and `github pr_checkout` no longer clone the checkout into a worktree path inside it, such as `.worktrees/<name>`. The clone copied the destination into itself until the path was too long (can1357/oh-my-pi#16076): on a Windows Dev Drive it ran past the bash timeout and left a directory thousands of levels deep, and a later `du` on that directory crashed omp with `panic(tokio-rt-worker): Stack overflow`. Such a worktree now gets a plain checkout; worktrees outside the checkout are still cloned.
+
+## [18.12.2-fork.1] - 2026-10-19
+
+### Changed
+
+- Re-based the fork onto upstream v18.12.2. Upstream's scoped client tokens (`omp auth-gateway serve --clients=<file>`) work alongside the fork's managed users and pools: a client token is never an admin (management routes answer `403`), cannot read `/v1/usage` or `/v1/credentials/check`, and its requests are audited under the client's name.
+
+## [18.9.2-fork.1] - 2026-10-12
+
+### Changed
+
+- Re-based the fork onto upstream v18.9.2. `omp update` on a fork build still installs from the fork's GitHub releases, now through upstream's verified binary installer, and the startup update check skips source checkouts and manager-installed copies as upstream's does. The auth gateway leaves `disabledProviders` out of `/v1/usage`, `/v1/credentials/check` and its model catalog while keeping the fork's ACLs, account pools and keyless `models.yml` models.
+- The auth gateway serves upstream's OpenRouter routing variants (`openrouter/<id>:nitro`, `:floor`, dated ids) under the requested id; a model ACL deny rule on `<id>` also denies its variants.
+
+## [18.6.1-fork.3] - 2026-10-11
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Models discovered through a custom `models.yml` provider (`discovery: openai-models-list` or `proxy`) now take the reasoning levels the endpoint advertises on `/v1/models`: OpenRouter's `reasoning.supported_efforts` (with `default_effort` and `mandatory`) or the omp auth-gateway's `thinking_efforts`. OpenAI-shaped rows send the chosen level as `reasoning_effort`. A gateway serving Claude Opus 5.5 under its own provider name now offers `max`. Before, `openai-models-list` stopped at `high` (at `xhigh` when the matched reference already sent `reasoning_effort`), and `proxy` offered `max` on OpenAI-shaped rows without sending any `reasoning_effort`.
